I just realized that it would be way smarter to: 
1. store every permit generated for every bounty hunter in our database (also useful for our audits)
2. Pull all of these into the dApp in a single database read call. 
3. Run every one of those through the already implemented function that checks if the permit is claimable
@0xcodercrane what do you think about the database side?
@whilefoo maybe it's best to hold off on this bounty until we figure that out. It might be much simpler (and superior) to implement it this way.
